# Line endings are pinned here rather than left to config, because config is
# per-machine and .gitattributes travels with the repo. Git for Windows ships
# core.autocrlf=true in its SYSTEM config, which is invisible to
# `git config --global --list` and silently rewrites LF to CRLF the next time
# git touches a working tree. That has already corrupted 552 files in the
# the parent project repo on this fleet, including a signing key.
#
# Everything is LF, including the .cmd launchers. That is deliberate and
# verified: the batch launchers in bin\ were written with LF and run correctly
# on Windows 11 as-is, so there is no reason to introduce a second line-ending
# convention for three files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, so git never tries to normalise them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.exe binary
